  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1250 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nUpper ridge axis extends across the forecast area Monday with\ndecreasing rain chances and temps well above seasonal normals.\nMost guidance does maintain low rain chances primarily south of\nInterstate 40 but any coverage is expected to remain low.\n\nThe pattern across the southern Plains transitions on Tuesday as\nstronger flow aloft spreads downstream of a slow moving mid level\ntrough over the southwest CONUS. This trough will gather the\nremnant of tropical system Polo and spread the deep moisture \nplume eastward across the Plains. The persistent trend has been \nfor a slower trough advance with the higher rain chances now \nfocused in the Wednesday through Thursday time frame. Expect \nmultiple corridors of heavy rainfall to develop in or near the \nforecast area through mid week. A window of severe weather \npotential may also develop within the strengthening wind fields, \nhowever uncertainty also remains in specific details at this time \nrange. The slow moving upper trough may have lingering effects \ninto Friday, but once it pushes east of the region then dry \nweather will return. Potential for a stronger cold front next \nweekend.",
